# Formatting

There is no Prettier/ESLint print-width in this project. Do **not** wrap as if the limit were 80 characters.

- Target line width is **about 120 characters**.
- Keep **method calls** and **method definitions** on one line unless they would exceed ~120 characters.
- Keep **variable assignments** (including string constants) on one line unless they would exceed ~120 characters.
- **Object literals** stay one property per line when they have multiple properties. A call that takes an object can stay on one line up through the opening `{`, then properties wrap.
- Do not split a call’s arguments onto separate lines just because there are multiple arguments, if the full call fits.
- Imports with several named bindings may stay multiline.
